  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HLP/ Human Resources for Health (HRH) Activity Award</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Haiti):  The Health Leadership Project / Human Resources for Health (HLP/HRH) award will support the Government of Haiti&apos;s (GOH) Ministry of Health (MOH) to improve planning and management related to two essential functions: 1) Governance; and 2) Human Resources for Health (HRH). This award is USAID&apos;s primary investment toward ensuring the Government of Haiti (GOH) continues the implementation of the HRH strategy and implements the HRH transition plan of USG-supported workers to the GOH budget. . .Using FY 2022 funds, specific interventions include:.Support to the MOH Department of Human Resources with the implementation of the National Human Resources Plan..Support to the MOH in the consolidation and implementation of the Special Statute of the Public Service for Health in collaboration with the Office De Management et Des Ressources Humaines and other actors in the health sector.Support the MOH to strengthen human resource management.Support the review of the transition plan in collaboration with all stakeholders including Global Fund..Assist the MOH in the establishment and implementation of the Operational Workforce Planning Unit..Improve the availability of government-controlled health human resources for sustainable HIV services through a viable transition plan.. .The Centre de Formation et d&apos;Encadrement Technique, the implementing partner of this award, has collaborated with Management Science for Health throughout the first two years of the activity to acquire the technical skills and managerial capacities enabling them becoming direct recipients of the transition award from USAID in April 2022. The award supports the USG&apos;s goal to build local capacity and sustainability of its investments in Haiti. .</narrative>
  </description>
